+
+Research, implementation, and validation
+----------------------------------------
+Equation and Taylor derivation
+------------------------------
+- Verified by direct multiplication that the original Bargmann equation maps
+  to z^2 Psi''+(B1+B2 z)Psi'+(B3+qz)Psi=0 with
+  B1=2 conjugate(F)/V, B2=2 hbar*omega0/V, B3=-2E/V, q=2F/V.
+- Kept the distinction between independent algebraic continuation parameters
+  and the physical slice q=conjugate(B1), B2 real.
+- Direct coefficient extraction gives
+  B1(n+1)c_(n+1)+[n(n-1)+B2*n+B3]c_n+q*c_(n-1)=0.
+- With A1=B2+B3, A2=2+2B2+B3, A3=6+3B2+B3:
+  c1=-B3/B1
+  c2=[B3*A1-q*B1]/[2*B1^2]
+  c3=[q*B1*(A2+2B3)-B3*A1*A2]/[6*B1^3]
+  c4=[A3*B3*A1*A2-q*B1*A3*(A2+2B3)
+      -3*q*B1*B3*A1+3*q^2*B1^2]/[24*B1^4].
+- Physical formulas were independently simplified using
+  d_n=(V/2)n(n-1)+hbar*omega0*n, R_n=E-d_n, g=|F|^2.
+- An independent SymPy application of the differential operator cancels
+  z^0 through z^3 exactly.  The first residual of the polynomial truncated at
+  c4 is z^4, whose cancellation requires the omitted c5.
+
+Infinity derivation
+-------------------
+- With z=t^2 and Y(t)=Psi(t^2), derived
+  t^2 Y''+[(2B2-1)t+2B1/t]Y'+(4B3+4q t^2)Y=0.
+- Integer powers of z^-1 are not closed for q != 0; the correct scale is
+  t^-n=z^(-n/2).
+- For a chosen s=sqrt(-q), a_sigma=2*sigma*s,
+  p=1/2-B2, r=p/2, and
+  C=p^2+(2B2-2)p+4B3, derived
+  u_(m+1)={[m(m+1)+C]u_m+2*a_sigma*B1*u_(m-1)
+           +2*B1*(p-m+2)u_(m-2)}/[2*a_sigma*(m+1)].
+- The first coefficients are
+  u1=C/(2*a_sigma),
+  u2=B1/2+C(C+2)/(8*a_sigma^2),
+  u3=C(C+2)(C+6)/(48*a_sigma^3)
+     +B1(3C+6+4p)/(12*a_sigma).
+- Independent symbolic substitution cancels reduced orders
+  t^0, t^-1, and t^-2.  Truncation at u3 first leaves t^-3=z^-3/2,
+  which is cancelled by u4.
+- No convergence or uniform-error claim is made.
+
+Branches and sectors
+--------------------
+- On a simply connected sector, compatible logarithms define
+  sqrt(-qz)=exp(Log(-qz)/2) and z^r=exp(r Log z).
+- sigma is dominant for Re(sigma*sqrt(-qz))>0 and subdominant for the
+  opposite sign.
+- Manuscript convention: Re sqrt(-qz)=0 are Stokes rays (equal exponential
+  magnitude); Im sqrt(-qz)=0 are anti-Stokes rays (maximal growth/decay).
+  The terminology is explicitly noted as non-universal.
+- One circuit changes sqrt(z) to -sqrt(z), multiplies z^r by exp(2*pi*i*r),
+  changes z^(-n/2) by (-1)^n, and swaps the sigma labels coherently.
+
+Exact boundary
+--------------
+- At F=conjugate(F)=0, B1=q=0 and the equation is Euler.
+- The indicial equation is rho(rho-1)+B2*rho+B3=0.
+- Since ||z^n||_B^2=n!, the normalized eigenpairs are
+  Psi_n=z^n/sqrt(n!) and
+  E_n=hbar*omega0*n+(V/2)n(n-1).
+- For n>0, Psi_n(0)=0.  Thus c0=1, division by B1, and the q != 0
+  square-root scale all fail at the exact boundary.  No continuity of the
+  excited-state normalization is claimed as F -> 0.
